## Model card

- **Name:** Grok 5 — identity unconfirmed
- **Short description:** Slug `grok-5` appears in model-queue.md (curated Overall 62.5). No public model card, technical report, benchmark table, or repository found in fetched sources for a model literally named "grok-5"; xAI's public releases at research date are the Grok 4.x family. This report draws on Grok 4.5 (benchlm #41/954, 63.27) and Grok 4.7 (media.x.ai model card) as the closest xAI references, explicitly flagged as not grok-5-specific.
- **Provider / access:** xAI API, Grok app, Grok Build, Cursor, OpenRouter (per opencode.ai data for Grok 4.x).
- **Release / knowledge:** Grok 4.5 released 2026-07-16 (llm-stats); Grok 4.7 model card dated 2026-09-21 (media.x.ai). Grok 5 release date/knowledge cutoff not established from public sources.
- **IDs:** `grok-5` (model-queue slug); xAI public IDs observed: grok-4-5, grok-4-6, grok-4-7 (opencode.ai data). No confirmed `grok-5` API ID found.
- **Context window:** Grok 4.x family: 500K (opencode.ai data for grok-4.5/4.6/4.7). Grok-5-specific context undisclosed.
- **Modalities:** Grok 4.5: text+image in, text out (opencode.ai data); Grok 4.7: text+image+pdf in. Grok-5-specific modalities undisclosed.
- **Reasoning:** yes (xAI models are reasoning-capable); tool calls yes.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-16):** Grok 4.5: $2.00/M input, $6.00/M output (the-decoder.com; opencode.ai data); Grok 4.7 same. Grok-5 pricing undisclosed.
- **Architecture:** xAI proprietary; trained on tens of thousands of Nvidia GB300 GPUs (grok-4.5 per the-decoder.com); parameter count undisclosed for grok-4.x/5.

### Raw benchmarks found (Grok 4.x family — NOT grok-5-specific)

Grok 4.5 (xAI launch post / benchlm.ai / the-decoder.com / llm-stats / vals.ai):

Agent / tool use:
- Terminal-Bench 2.1: **83.3%** (xAI launch post) — nearly matching GPT-5.5 (83.4%), trailing Fable 5 (84.3%) by 1 pt
- SWE-Bench Pro: **64.7%** (xAI launch post)
- deepSWE: **53%** (xAI launch post)
- Terminal-Bench 2.1 (Vals): **67.8%** (Vals AI)
- GDPval-AA: **44.2%** (AA) / **1430 Elo** (AA)
- AA Agentic Index: **42.1%** (benchlm)

Reasoning / knowledge:
- GPQA Diamond: **93.1%** (AA-GPQA Diamond) / **92.9%** (Vals AI GPQA Diamond leaderboard)
- MMLU-Pro: **89.2%** (Vals AI MMLU Pro leaderboard)
- HLE: **42.7%** (AA-HLE)
- ARC-AGI-2: **52.6%** / ARC-AGI-3: **0.3%** / ARC-AGI-1: **85.67%** (ARC Prize official)
- AA-Omniscience: index 25.3%, accuracy 51.6%, hallucination rate 54.1% (benchlm)
- AA-LCR: **79.3%** (benchlm)
- CritPt: **15.4%** (benchlm)
- Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index: **38.8%** (benchlm)

Coding:
- SWE-Bench Pro: **64.7%** — see above
- SWE Multilingual: **78%** (Cursor)
- CursorBench 3.2: **66.7%**
- VulcanBench v3: **89.9%**

Long context:
- 500K context (opencode.ai data; llm-stats); AA-LCR 79.3% moderate; no public full-window retrieval curve.

Instruction following: Not isolated for grok-4.5 in fetched sources.

### Conflicting results noted

- **No distinct grok-5 evidence exists** — all xAI figures above are grok-4.x family (primarily grok-4.5). Attributing them to grok-5 would be speculative; they are reported here only as the closest xAI reference with explicit caveats.
- **Grok 4.5 hallucination rate:** AA-Omniscience hallucination rate 54.1% vs accuracy 51.6% — model knows more but is more confident when wrong (the-decoder.com).
- **Price/performance:** Grok 4.5 $2/$6 per M (~4.2× fewer tokens than Opus 4.8 on SWE-Bench Pro per the-decoder.com) — cheap in its tier.

